WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers&nbsp;
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér. Dr. Papers.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:12.840
Earlier we talked about two text to video systems,&nbsp;
Google’s amazing Imagen Video, and also NVIDIA’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:19.380
videomaker AI. However, to the best of my&nbsp;
knowledge, as of today, there are no easy ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:26.040
of trying them out. Now, before we start, just to&nbsp;
make sure: tons of video AI-related techniques are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:32.880
available right now, many of them for free, I’ll&nbsp;
show you those, but their text to video system is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.220
still in testing phase as of the making of this&nbsp;
video. I will show you some results for that too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:44.040
however, good news, it is also expected&nbsp;
to open to the public within a few weeks.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:51.120
So this is Runway. They had a hand in the creation&nbsp;
of the amazing free text to image AI tool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:57.840
Stable Diffusion, and they have an incredible&nbsp;
creative suite for all kinds of AI-based video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.780
magic. I will tell you about text to video&nbsp;
in a moment. First, they introduced Gen-1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.580
this is their video to video system.&nbsp;
Here you can take a video of yourself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:15.600
then choose a style, and bam! You have a&nbsp;
completely new, stylized video. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.300
just this one feature makes it worth&nbsp;
trying this system as it has of uses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:28.860
but it has a ton of other really creative modes&nbsp;
as well. We can mask out a dog, and only change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:35.520
that part of the video, which will get tracked as&nbsp;
this good boy moves around in the scene. Lovely.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:42.300
It can also remove the background behind us&nbsp;
in a video, and track both the foreground and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:48.120
background over time. Also, if we have an image&nbsp;
that we would like to expand, it can also perform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:54.360
text to image with the appropriate constraints&nbsp;
and it will expand it in a way that we often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.880
can’t even tell that something happened&nbsp;
here. We can also erase parts of an image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:07.080
and replace them with a text prompt as well.&nbsp;
Now, wait a second, these two are image-related&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:14.160
operations. But we are talking about videos&nbsp;
here. So what is going on? Well, one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.940
these photos can be used for Gen-1 as a style&nbsp;
to a previously existing video, or even better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:28.140
get this. You can also create a video by adding&nbsp;
a few photos that were taken a few seconds apart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:35.700
and like magic, it creates a video out of them.&nbsp;
Yes, that means understanding what these photos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:43.500
depict, and synthesizing every pixel of every&nbsp;
image between these photos. Absolutely incredible.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.660
And their suite is full of features we&nbsp;
haven’t even discussed yet. Colorization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.940
with or without using a text prompt,&nbsp;
blurring faces while tracking them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:59.940
and so much more. Now, this is what you’ve&nbsp;
been waiting for! Onwards to text to video.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:06.000
Note once again that this is still in testing&nbsp;
phase, and will hopefully be part of the main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:12.060
suite within a few weeks. I was lucky enough&nbsp;
to be able to try it and it did not disappoint.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:20.040
Before you ask, the answer is yes, of course&nbsp;
I generated a video of Fellow Scholars holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:26.640
on to their papers. Wow! I was told that it&nbsp;
is not yet that good in generating humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:33.360
and if this is the not good, I can only imagine&nbsp;
how good the launch version will look like! This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:40.140
is excellent. My first text to video experience&nbsp;
ever. Loving it. What a time to be alive!

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:46.980
And here is my other favorite, fluid simulations,&nbsp;
well, in this case, video footage of splashing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.840
liquids which also worked really well.&nbsp;
Some of the results were not as great,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:58.560
so a little cherry picking was necessary here,&nbsp;
but in the end I got some really tasty results.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:04.560
I was also told that the system is improved every&nbsp;
week, so by the time you are watching this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:11.640
it will likely have improved a great deal already.&nbsp;
The current system supports videos up to 1500x900&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:19.260
in resolution. Not bad! And that is easily&nbsp;
good enough so that some folks are already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:25.740
creating incredibly good movies with it that&nbsp;
are several minutes long. Imagine that soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:31.560
every creative person will have access to&nbsp;
such an amazing system and can let their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.840
imaginations run wild. All of us!&nbsp;
This is the future of video making.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:42.420
So if you wish to try this suite, note&nbsp;
once again - text to video is coming later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.940
you can sign up for free on Runway’s website.&nbsp;
The link is in the video description.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.140
I will note that Runway is a previous&nbsp;
sponsor of Two Minute Papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:57.540
and had nothing to do with this video apart from&nbsp;
letting my try it and answering my questions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:03.780
This is their first time seeing it too. So,&nbsp;
what do you think? What will you make with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.340
this? Let me know in the comments below,&nbsp;
and for now, let the experiments begin!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.900
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

